nd Drug Administration, 2018), and nedosiran (2023) (U.S. Food and Drug Administration, 2023b). This list is illustrative rather than exhaustive. GalNAc mediates hepatocyte recognition through ASGPR, whereas RNA interference occurs intracellularly (Nair et al., 2014; Li et al., 2024; Springer and Dowdy, 2018). Peptide-vectored ODCs have been investigated for muscle delivery; Pip6-PMO enhanced exon skipping in preclinical DMD models (Betts et al., 2012). The clinical PPMO programme SRP-5051 was discontinued in November 2024 following prolonged hypomagnesemia and reduced eGFR in some participants (Sarepta, 2024). These observations do not establish a class-wide toxicity mechanism. Antibody- and aptamer-based oligonucleotide delivery approaches are also discussed (Roberts et al., 2020); a single development-stage label is not assigned to these heterogeneous classes. Endosomal escape remains an important delivery limitation for many ODCs: only a small percentage of\n\n---\n\nFrontiers in Pharmacology  \n07  \nfrontiersin.org\n\nMorceau et al.  \n10.3389/fphar.2026.1970939--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSHP609-302 | Clinical Trial Summary (https://clinicaltrials.takeda.com/study-detail/5f6b5fd54db2bf003ab46df0)\nciteturn182search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Participants who were not previously treated with idursulfase-IT in study HGT-HIT-094 will begin participation in this study at the start of the Initial Treatment Phase (i.e. the first 12 months) of this study. ... Participants will participate in this extension study for a duration of 5 years of treatment unless they discontinue the study or Shire discontinues the study.\n\nAll participants in this study wil be treated wth intrathecal indursulfase-IT in conjunctin with Elaprase treatment. The study is intended to provide ongoing treatment with idursulfase-IT for participants who received idursulfase-IT in study HGT-HIT-094 and to initiate treatment with 